/target

# Local agent tooling state. The worktrees are nested git repositories, which
# `git add -A` will happily stage as a gitlink to a commit that exists on one
# machine only.
#
# The contents are ignored rather than the directory itself: git does not
# descend into an ignored directory, so `/.claude` would make the negation
# below dead and `settings.json` unshareable.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json

# The benchmark's registry recording: hundreds of megabytes of tarballs, taken
# by `./benches/bench.sh --record` and replayed by every measuring run. Far too
# large to commit, and regenerable from the live registry by definition.
/benches/.mirror/
